      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Getting a speech recognizer and making a recognition request",
      "normalizedSource": "Getting a speech recognizer and making a recognition request",
      "sourceHash": "f1b6e8cd8692eea0081fb080918f0b0bdef7592b94691ceac427c1b57ae04241",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Listing 1.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nfunc recognizeFile(url: URL) {\n    // Create a speech recognizer associated with the user's default language.\n    guard let myRecognizer = SFSpeechRecognizer() else {\n        // The system doesn't support the user's default language.\n        return\n    }\n    \n    guard myRecognizer.isAvailable else {\n        // The recognizer isn't available.\n        return\n    }\n    \n    // Create and execute a speech recognition request for the audio file at the URL.\n    let request = SFSpeechURLRecognitionRequest(url: url)\n    myRecognizer.recognitionTask(with: request) { (result, error) in\n        guard let result else {\n            // Recognition failed, so check the error for details and handle it.\n            return\n        }\n        \n        // Print the speech transcription with the highest confidence that the\n        // system recognized.\n        if result.isFinal {\n            print(result.bestTranscription.formattedString)\n        }\n    }\n}\n```",
      "documentTitle": "SFSpeechURLRecognitionRequest",
      "framework": "Speech",
      "ko": "",
